  "mathematical_route": [
    "Apply the generic relabeled-LU trajectory and admissibility lemmas to the exact rational factorization. Prefix pivots are legal because the prefix lower-factor entries have modulus at most1; actual pivot labels are the proved physical original-row rotation.",
    "At stage p+q the original-row permutation sends the target physical row to the same factor row. The unit-lower tail identity leaves the target upper diagonal, namely h_p(p+q).",
    "The complete LU factors have unit lower diagonal and strictly positive rational upper diagonal. The row permutation and both determinants are nonzero, so the original rational input is nonsingular.",
    "Use genuine admissible-prefix extension, not a claim that the seed suffix is legal. Its preserved target stage forces growth at least h_p(p+q), while the full universal bound gives equality.",
    "For p=0 use the identity of dimension q+1, with literal no-swap pivots shown admissible from identity LU. Its growth is1 by the proved zero-lower-band theorem.",
    "These explicit witnesses place sharpBound in the complete growthValues set. All other members are bounded by universal_growth, giving IsGreatest and the real supremum exactly."
  ],
  "numerical_computation": "Only the already held half_bounds_certificate uses LeanCert kernel interval arithmetic; all parameter-dependent recurrence, matrix, determinant and growth arguments are symbolic. No matrix enumeration is used in a proof.",
